y700-osk: do not activate the click stream while key clicks are off (y700 DRAFT, NOT APPLIED, 2026-10-16)

Osk::show() and Osk::click() call Sound::setActive(true) before play(), and play() drops the click when
the volume is 0. With key clicks switched off, every keyboard show and every key press still activates the
stream for the 10 s idle window (osk.cpp:134-137), which runs the whole speaker path on silence: PipeWire
starts the ALSA sink, the PCM and both DSP graphs run, both aw882xx amplifiers are powered (SUSPEND.md 2.2, 2.5, 5.5).
Skip the activation while the volume is 0; raising the volume and the next click activate it as before.
Screen-on only; no effect when key clicks are on. Not built, not tested.

diff --git a/linux/osk/src/sound.cpp b/linux/osk/src/sound.cpp
--- a/linux/osk/src/sound.cpp
+++ b/linux/osk/src/sound.cpp
@@ -180,6 +180,10 @@
 void Sound::setActive(bool on)
 {
     if (on == m_active) return;
+    // key clicks switched off: do not wake the speaker path (PCM, DSP graph, both amplifiers) only to
+    // play silence for the 10 s idle window (linux/audio/SUSPEND.md); the next click after the volume
+    // is raised again activates the stream as before
+    if (on && m_volume.load() <= 0) return;
     m_active = on;
     if (!m_stream) return;
     pw_thread_loop_lock(m_loop);
